Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Old Batavia Shoals
- Story & Context: When water patrols cut the solar grid at the 2091 Solstice rooftop blowout, Ren pulled a contact-mic'd Victorian music box from his satchel, keeping two thousand drenched revelers jumping to its fragile tinkling amidst the heavy smell of bruised guava and ozone. Bram plugged his drop-tuned baritone into an illicit hydro-battery right as the police spotlights washed over the crowd, dropping the heaviest half-time bounce the drowned district had ever registered on a seismograph. Before the patrol boats could breach the stairwell, Ren yelled through a bullhorn, "Tear the nautical map, we are dancing on the crest!" initiating a frantic sprint across bamboo rope bridges that became the scene's foundational myth.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: An album cover view of a submerged colonial clocktower poking out of sparkling azure waters under a fierce midday sun, mechanical brass gears and rusted music box tines spilling outward into a turquoise reef, raw folk-art lettering etched across the tide line.

Track 2: Brass Calipers Bleed Guava
- Story & Context: Written in the sweltering, damp attic of a scuttled cartography archive, the track began when Kiri traded three weeks of clean drinking water for a 19th-century Swiss cylinder chime salvaged from the drowned maritime library. Bram initially smashed his fist through the drywall in sheer fury over the wasted rations, but broke down weeping when Kiri played the tinkling melody over his detuned, swampy acoustic bassline. During the rooftop rehearsal, sweat dripped like condensation off the rusted fretboards into a bowl of sliced wild fruit as Kiri screamed into the condenser mic: "I traded my canteen for thirty teeth of tin!"
