Track 3: Who Drew This Border on the Tide?
- Story & Context: During the final week of the legendary 2091 heatwave, rival rooftop flotillas clashed over fishing rights until elder diver Mira hoisted a massive PA stack atop the Marina Spire and cranked this track at daybreak. The combination of frantic, carnival-bright steelpans, delicate music box arpeggios, and a skull-rattling rap-metal breakdown turned an imminent gang war into an exhausted, sun-blinded celebration across fifty anchored rafts. As the tide swallowed the municipal concrete seawall forever, Mira sprayed fermented palm wine over the moshers, roaring the refrain: "Salt washed the demarcation line right out of our jaws!"
